---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SecureFieldsCrumbs from '../../components/SecureFieldsCrumbs.astro';

const title = 'Support SLA | Secure Fields';
const description =
  'Support hours, target response times, and service availability for the Secure Fields Jira Cloud app by Inorganic Games LLC.';

// The commitments below are referenced throughout the page. Change them here and
// the whole document stays consistent — and keep them in sync with the Atlassian
// Marketplace vendor support profile.
const sla = {
  updated: 'August 22, 2026',
  effective: 'August 22, 2026',
  timezone: 'Pacific Time (America/Los_Angeles)',
  hours: '9:00 AM to 5:00 PM',
  days: 'Monday through Friday',
  standardResponse: '24 business hours',
  urgentResponse: '8 business hours',
};

const holidays = [
  { name: "New Year's Day", rule: 'January 1' },
  { name: 'Memorial Day', rule: 'Last Monday in May' },
  { name: 'Independence Day', rule: 'July 4 (observed on the nearest weekday when it falls on a weekend)' },
  { name: 'Labor Day', rule: 'First Monday in September' },
  { name: 'Thanksgiving', rule: 'Fourth Thursday in November, and the Friday following' },
  { name: 'Christmas Eve and Christmas Day', rule: 'December 24 and December 25' },
  { name: "New Year's Eve", rule: 'December 31' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <SecureFieldsCrumbs current="sla" />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-signal">Support</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl tracking-wide text-bone md:text-5xl">Support Service Level Agreement</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
      Inorganic Games LLC &mdash; Secure Fields<br />
      Effective: {sla.effective} &middot; Last updated: {sla.updated}
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">1. What this document is</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This Service Level Agreement ("SLA") is the Support Policy and SLA referenced in our
          <a href="/secure-fields/terms" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">Terms of Service</a>
          (Sections 5.1 and 5.2). It describes when we are available, how quickly we aim to reply, and
          what falls outside the scope of support.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          It applies to customers with an active paid subscription to Secure Fields through the Atlassian
          Marketplace. Evaluations, trials, and any beta features get best-effort support with no
          committed response time &mdash; Section 18 of our Terms disclaims any SLA or support obligation
          for Trials and Betas, and the targets below do not extend to them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">2. How to reach support</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Email
          <a href="mailto:support@inorganicgames.com" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">support@inorganicgames.com</a>.
          Email is our only support channel; we do not operate a phone line or live chat.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">To let us act on the first reply, please include:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>your Jira site URL,</li>
          <li>the name of the affected Secure Text field and, if you have it, the issue key,</li>
          <li>what you expected to happen and what happened instead,</li>
          <li>whether the problem affects one user, one project, or the whole site.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-bone">Never include a protected value in a support request.</strong> We have no
          way to read the values your app stores, and we do not want a copy. The same goes for anything
          regulated &mdash; protected health information, financial account numbers, or government ID
          numbers belong only inside the app's protected field, never in an email, a screenshot, a field
          name, or an issue summary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">3. Hours of operation</h2>
        <dl class="mt-3 space-y-4">
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-signal">Days</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">{sla.days}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-signal">Hours</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">{sla.hours}, {sla.timezone}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-signal">Closed</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">Weekends and the holidays listed in Section 7</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You can write to us at any hour. Requests that arrive outside these hours are treated as
          arriving when we next open, and the response clock starts then.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">4. Target response times</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          "Response" means a substantive reply from a person who has read your request &mdash; a question, a
          diagnosis, a workaround, or a fix. It is not an automated acknowledgement. These are targets we
          measure ourselves against during the hours of operation above, not guarantees, and this SLA
          carries no service credits.
        </p>
        <dl class="mt-5 space-y-5">
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-signal">Urgent &mdash; {sla.urgentResponse}</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">
              The app is unusable across your site; a protected value is visible to someone your rules do
              not authorize; a protected value is unreachable by someone your rules do authorize; or a
              suspected security vulnerability (see Section 6).
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-signal">Standard &mdash; {sla.standardResponse}</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1">
              Everything else: configuration and setup questions, unexpected behavior with a workaround,
              audit log questions, billing questions, documentation gaps, and feature requests.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We categorize incoming requests ourselves, and will tell you if we read a request differently
          than you did. Response targets say nothing about how long a fix takes: some issues are answered
          and closed in one reply, and others need a code change and a Marketplace release. We will keep
          you updated as work progresses rather than going quiet.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">5. Service availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Secure Fields runs entirely on Atlassian's Forge platform. We operate no servers, no databases,
          and no network endpoints of our own, and the app sends no data outside Atlassian's platform.
          The practical consequence is that the app's availability is the availability of your Jira Cloud
          site and of the Forge platform underneath it, both of which Atlassian operates and covers under
          its own agreements with you.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We therefore do not publish a separate uptime percentage for the app and do not offer service
          credits for downtime &mdash; doing either would be claiming credit for infrastructure we do not
          run. For live platform status, see
          <a href="https://status.atlassian.com" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim" rel="noopener">status.atlassian.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          What we do commit to: responding on the schedule above when the app itself is at fault, and
          telling you plainly when the cause sits with the platform rather than with us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">6. Security vulnerability reports</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Report suspected vulnerabilities privately to
          <a href="mailto:support@inorganicgames.com" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">support@inorganicgames.com</a>
          rather than in a public forum. We treat these as Urgent ({sla.urgentResponse} target
          acknowledgement), we will not take action against good-faith security research, and we will keep
          you informed through remediation. Please do not include a proof-of-concept payload containing
          real protected data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">7. Observed holidays</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Support is closed on these United States holidays:</p>
        <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3">
          {
            holidays.map((h) => (
              <div>
                <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-signal">{h.name}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1">{h.rule}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Urgent requests that arrive on a holiday are picked up on the next business day. If a
          vulnerability report lands over a long holiday weekend, send it anyway &mdash; we would rather see
          it early.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">8. What support does not cover</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            Outages, degradation, or maintenance of Jira Cloud or the Forge platform. Those are
            Atlassian's to resolve; we will help you identify them as such.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-bone">Recovery of protected values.</strong> Protected values are stored only
            in Forge storage on your site. They are deliberately absent from Jira's own backups and
            exports, and we have no access to them. If a value is overwritten or deleted by a user with
            edit access, or lost when the app is uninstalled, we cannot restore it. See the
            <a href="/secure-fields/docs" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">Setup &amp; Usage Guide</a>
            for the backup tradeoffs this creates.
          </li>
          <li>
            Configuration you control: permission rules naming a group or project role that does not
            exist, users removed from a group, or a field added to the wrong screen. We will help you
            diagnose these, but the fix is in your Jira site.
          </li>
          <li>
            Third-party apps, browser extensions, custom scripts, or integrations that interact with the
            app, and any Jira functionality unrelated to Secure Fields.
          </li>
          <li>
            Feature requests. We read every one and they shape the roadmap, but no delivery date is
            committed here.
          </li>
          <li>Use of the app outside the Permitted Use defined in our Terms of Service.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">9. Changes to this SLA</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update this SLA to reflect new features or changing practices, with notice to you. Any
          change takes effect going forward only, and will not materially reduce our overall support
          obligations during a subscription term you have already paid for. This mirrors Section 19.6 of
          our Terms of Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-wide text-bone">10. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Inorganic Games LLC<br />
          <a href="mailto:support@inorganicgames.com" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">support@inorganicgames.com</a>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          See also
          <a href="/secure-fields/support" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">Support</a>,
          <a href="/secure-fields/terms" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">Terms of Service</a>, and the
          <a href="/secure-fields/security" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-signal-dim">Security Overview</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
